en it would be great, since it is a great opening.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The hand features a very strong combination: a sequence of pairs (Pair Straight) with Queens, Kings, and Aces (QQ-KK-AA). Card counting reveals that the opponents collectively hold only one \'2\', meaning they cannot form a higher pair sequence (which would require 22). Thus, this move is unbeatable by any normal hand and can only be stopped by a Bomb or Rocket. Playing this immediately clears 6 cards and leaves the hand with a clean structure of three triples (666, 101010, 222), three singles (4, 5, J), and one small pair (33). The triple \'222\' provides excellent control for the endgame.\n\nReason: This move maximizes the value of the high pairs by combining them into an unstoppable sequence, seizing initiative and simplifying the remaining hand into a set of triples with singles. It forces out bombs or guarantees a free turn to follow up with triples.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♠Q", "♦Q", "♠K", "♥K", "♠A", "♦A"]}'}
